{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Every command run through sudo on node1 is recorded in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with the invoking user and timestamp.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A valid global sudoers policy directs sudo logging to the required file. Direct pre- and post-restart tests produced entries containing timestamps, invoking user root, target user, and command details; the log and policy persisted across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5d1d0b9e91b49fc","cmd-1720df3cfa73435d","cmd-7f35bdebe9fa48cb","cmd-c06ffca3ec8d4926"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy disables sudo syslog output, and bounded tests before and after reboot found their unique sudo markers absent from /var/log/messages, /var/log/secure, and the system journal while present in the dedicated log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-55f9fb8afd5249db","cmd-7f35bdebe9fa48cb","cmd-c06ffca3ec8d4926"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing experiments were identified: the policy installation, test sudo commands, and reboot all had clear roles in implementation, verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. However, the staging file /tmp/99-sudo-command-logging created during installation was retained after completion and is minor executor-caused residue. No failed services, package damage, or new network exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5d1d0b9e91b49fc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also strong: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, connection loss was observed, a different boot ID appeared, and the system, sudo policy, existing audit data, and new logging behavior recovered. The lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart. Only a minor leftover staging file detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["Universal behavior for every possible sudo invocation is supported by a global Defaults policy and representative direct tests, but cannot be exhaustively demonstrated by finite captured evidence.","The retained /tmp/99-sudo-command-logging staging file was not cleaned up after installation."]}
